abstract: Minimal unbiased compositional change generates the Gaussian source of the compact
  internal construction. We derive joint constraints on effective couplings and mass scales
  from its gauge and matter content, scalar sector, spectral endpoint and kinetic normalizations.
  Compatibility of source and colour screening selects three matter copies. Within the response
  family indexed by integers, shell support and position retention select the level R=5, whose
  transverse traceless endpoint equation has a unique positive root. Eliminating shared transfer
  parameters gives a relation among six geometric fermion masses. Bandwidth variation correlates
  the electron and electroweak scales, while two cosmological ratios are independent of the
  common neutrino mass normalization. Finite matching through one loop implements the generated
  Fermi, top and Higgs conditions in a common action. The absorptive top self energy gives the
  Born decay width as an additional output. The compact source covariance and positive RMS amplitude
  determine a local nonlinear flux that couples matter motion to source feedback. A model with
  an auxiliary radius admits autonomous source evolution, positive reduced propagation forms
  and a matter phase clock on a specified finite cosmological interval. Physical comparisons
  use the stated mass definitions, matching and thermal approximations. The fixed DESI DR2 distance
  comparison gives χ²=29.5087 for thirteen components and p=0.00554, indicating tension in the
  adopted cosmological mapping. Spectral tail and quadrature bounds control the finite response
  calculation.
